    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        The useful split in this category is not features, it is <strong>where the
        work runs and who can read it</strong>. Everything else (how the panes are
        arranged, which agents are wired up) moves in a release. That does not.
      </p>

      {/* Six columns cannot fit a phone, so the box scrolls rather than the
          page: at 390px the table forced the document to 712px wide and every
          section of the article inherited a horizontal scrollbar. `tabindex`
          because a scroll box that only a pointer can reach is not reachable. */}
